  "answer": "To reduce the risk of excessive absorption losses in multi-layer optics, it has been proposed to deploy MP-DQN with exponential reward and Lagrangian regularisation for multi-layer optical system design (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769). This is achieved through a mechanism using an MP-DQN architecture with separate *g* and *f* networks: the *g* network proposes a continuous thickness for each discrete material, while the *f* network evaluates Q-values for each material-thickness pair (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769). This architecture allows for the joint optimisation of discrete materials and continuous thickness parameters in one optimisation loop (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769)."
